\ Module A's stored quotation calls `b-only`, which only module B exports
\ and A never imports. A stamped body's module scope is authoritative: a
\ module-owned name outside it resolves nowhere, so the call must fail with
\ an unknown-word error, matching the interpreter, instead of resolving B's
\ export through the module-cache scan or B's compiled function through the
\ bare-name jit_dispatch sweep.

use { a-quot: a-tag: } "fixtures/own_module_image_scan_unknown_a.1z" ;
use { b-tag: } "fixtures/own_module_image_scan_unknown_b.1z" ;

a-tag print-line
b-tag print-line
a-quot call print-line
